 put that on top  and then give it a stir i'll get your  door yeah i just use a splash of oil  what i love about recipes like this is  there's this there's not a lot of work  that goes into it it's just a lot of  time and a lot of a lot of love right  absolutely  you gotta have a passion for it and  that's one thing it's a blessing that  i've had the opportunity to do that i  also use you gotta cook it down  chicken broth okay so pour that in the  consistency is what you're looking for  is to make sure that you have plenty of  liquids in this  and you can use chicken broth and water  about four cups of water is as well so  okay um pour that in  and  we'll give it a stir give it a stir this  is the most important ingredient it is  uh white distilled vinegar get about a  half cup of that so bring it to a simmer  turn the heat to low put the lid on it  and then four hours later you've got  voila we've got some delicious collard  greens let's see how they turned out  now does your family love this stuff  they do i actually keep  bags in the freezer so they have them  available whenever they want them  awesome they freeze very well you can  find all these ingredients at your local  smiths thank you so much for watching  thank you for shopping we'll see you  next time thank you uh thanks so much  for being with me it's been an honor  thank you all right bye bye everybody  thank you to smith's food and drug for  sponsoring this segment make sure to  visit their website for more information  it's right there on your screen mercedes  over to you
 

